WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.240
When you see some of the monsters&nbsp;
and entities they try to contain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.600
it’s easy to think of The SCP Foundation as&nbsp;
“the good guys.” And granted, when you observe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.480
the magnitude of threats like the Scarlet&nbsp;
King, it’s hard for anyone to not look like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.120
a downright moral paragon in comparison.&nbsp;
But the Foundation aren’t always knights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:24.720
in shining armor – sometimes, they themselves&nbsp;
have committed horrific atrocities in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:30.720
keep their supernatural subjects under wraps, and&nbsp;
keep the rest of us safe from anomalous terror.&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.520
Nowhere is that more clear than a&nbsp;
deadly incident that occurred in 2010.&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.440
The Foundation had been aware of&nbsp;
the Slow Burn Sloth for decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.400
and many believe that the entity has existed&nbsp;
for as long as human beings have consumed visual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:51.760
media. Movies, TV, web pages, and even print&nbsp;
media, like books and magazines, are vulnerable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:58.240
Technically speaking, the name “SCP–2774” refers&nbsp;
to whatever visual medium is currently holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:08.000
the true entity, known as SCP–2774–A. Thankfully,&nbsp;
SCP–2774–A has never made it onto the Internet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.920
where it could do truly catastrophic damage, but&nbsp;
the Foundation has prepared for that possibility.&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.120
They’ve invented a software&nbsp;
program, Webcrawler A03G32,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.540
designed to constantly monitor all forms of online&nbsp;
visual media for an appearance of SCP–2774–A.&nbsp;

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:34.960
So, what is SCP–2774–A? What could possibly&nbsp;
be so scary that even a picture of it leaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.120
onto the internet could potentially lead&nbsp;
to the collapse of human civilization?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:48.240
Simply put, SCP–2774–A is this image of an unknown&nbsp;
humanoid entity in a bizarre sloth costume.&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.520
While this picture may seem harmless, that’s&nbsp;
only because it’s black and white, and any red or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.880
green hues have been neutralized from the image.&nbsp;
Anyone who isn’t red-green color blind and somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:06.560
accidentally sees the true version of SCP–2774–A&nbsp;
has a fate far worse than death in store for them.&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.440
This is the same fate that would befall almost&nbsp;
the entire population of the Northern Canadian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.960
town of Harper Ridge in 2010. The residents of&nbsp;
this small township were waking up and going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:22.080
about their morning. Some were getting ready&nbsp;
for work, others enjoying a leisurely breakfast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:27.600
in front of the television set. All of those&nbsp;
affected had unknowingly made the deadly mistake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.760
of watching the local news that morning.
While the anchor droned on about some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.360
local economic statistics and delivered a dry&nbsp;
advertisement for an upcoming town festival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:43.520
the familiar image of something in a sloth&nbsp;
costume appeared briefly on the set behind him.&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:48.000
Most of the Harper Ridge Residents who viewed&nbsp;
the broadcast didn’t even notice the sloth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.040
but in that fateful instant, almost&nbsp;
every single one of them was doomed.&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.560
The Slow Burn Sloth doesn’t always affect everyone&nbsp;
who sees it. Foundation scientists have found that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.760
it generally only affects 40% of people exposed&nbsp;
to it, and doesn’t affect those suffering from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.880
color-blindness at all. However, one of the more&nbsp;
frightening details about the sloth – which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:14.000
classified as a memetic image SCP, for its&nbsp;
ability to spread and appear randomly almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:20.160
anywhere – is that it grows more powerful and more&nbsp;
contagious with every living victim it affects.&nbsp;

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.560
After claiming a significant number of&nbsp;
new victims – say, from a small Canadian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:32.080
town – SCP–2774–A’s infection rate&nbsp;
can rise to as high as 60%, or beyond.&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.440
The residents of Harper Ridge made their own&nbsp;
predator deadlier without even knowing it.&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:43.280
At a nearby Foundation facility, units were&nbsp;
already mobilizing. It was too late for those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.000
who had already seen the Slow Burn Sloth,&nbsp;
but others could potentially be saved if the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:53.440
situation was contained quickly. In addition to&nbsp;
the Webcrawler constantly monitoring the internet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:58.400
the SCP Foundation also had a huge number of&nbsp;
dedicated teams scanning broadcasts worldwide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:05.120
for potential incidences of SCP–2774–A&nbsp;
exposure. When one of these teams detected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.440
the Sloth’s presence in Harper Ridge’s&nbsp;
morning newscast, and found that upwards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:15.200
of 4,000 civilians had already been exposed,&nbsp;
they knew that there was no time to waste.&nbsp;

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:20.640
Back in Harper Ridge, the situation was already&nbsp;
deteriorating. A few hours had passed since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:26.080
the broadcast, and those who were exposed were&nbsp;
beginning to experience strange symptoms already.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:32.080
First, it was a sense of tiredness and lethargy.&nbsp;
Then, an unusual heaviness to their body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:36.000
as though they were experiencing&nbsp;
sudden, extreme muscle fatigue.&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:42.800
People exposed to SCP–2774–A also experienced&nbsp;
clouded cognition – even thinking straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.200
became a real struggle. It was at this&nbsp;
point that the true effects of witnessing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:52.640
the Slow Burn Sloth began to take hold,&nbsp;
around six hours after initial exposure.&nbsp;

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:56.800
Little by little, the infected lost all&nbsp;
cognitive functions and higher-level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:02.160
decision-making abilities. Their bodies&nbsp;
still acted out basic movements very slowly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:07.840
seemingly just as a result of muscle memory,&nbsp;
but they had no control over what was going on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:14.480
They became, essentially, living zombies, trapped&nbsp;
in their own bodies and only dimly aware of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:19.200
This horrifying experience was completely&nbsp;
consistent with prior Foundation research&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:25.920
into the effects of viewing SCP–2774–A.
And in a twist almost crueler than permanent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:31.680
zombification, victims of the Slow Burn&nbsp;
Sloth are randomly allocated around 150&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:38.240
seconds of lucidity every 24 hours before&nbsp;
being forced back into their zombified state.&nbsp;

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:43.280
Just as 4,000 of Harper Ridge’s residents&nbsp;
were beginning to experience these effects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:47.280
all local communication channels to the&nbsp;
town were cut off by the Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.240
Well-equipped teams of mobile task force operators&nbsp;
began arriving on the scene shortly after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:57.440
accompanied by a number of containment units in&nbsp;
the form of buses and trucks. Luckily for them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.720
the zombified victims of the Slow Burn Sloth&nbsp;
were incredibly docile and compliant by nature.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:07.680
Shepherding all 4,000 of them into the containment&nbsp;
units was almost like working with cattle.&nbsp;

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.720
Some non-infected local residents attempted to&nbsp;
protest the sudden abduction of their zombified&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:16.880
loved ones. These residents were subdued&nbsp;
and either had their memories wiped with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:23.120
Foundation Amnestics, or were terminated on site.
Like with almost any conceivable situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:28.400
the SCP Foundation already had measures in&nbsp;
place for a mass exposure event like this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:34.000
All in all, a mere 4,000 was still on the&nbsp;
low end of the potential infection scale. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:40.080
4,000 victims were secretly taken to Site-116, a&nbsp;
Foundation testing site under the direction of Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.600
Martin and his second in command, Dr. Klara Chung.
There, they’d already been pursuing research on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.160
approximately 2,400 infected subjects&nbsp;
from prior incidents – including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.800
Foundation personnel who were accidentally&nbsp;
infected during the monitoring process.&nbsp;

00:06:54.800 --> 00:07:00.080
Thus far, it seemed that the condition caused&nbsp;
by witnessing the Slow Burn Sloth was incurable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:08.880
And with 6,400 known living victims situated at&nbsp;
Site-116, SCP–2774–A was at an unprecedented level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:14.000
of power. All site personnel were instructed&nbsp;
to proceed with caution, and carefully observe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:18.400
the behavior of their new test subjects.
Dr. Chung spearheaded the majority of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:23.280
hands-on research into the infected residents&nbsp;
of Harper Ridge and observed some interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:27.600
phenomena in the victim’s behavioral&nbsp;
patterns as the condition escalated.&nbsp;

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:32.720
The infected subjects, even in their largely&nbsp;
zombified state, developed an almost fanatically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:38.000
religious obsession with the image of the Slow&nbsp;
Burn Sloth. When left to their own devices, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:45.600
would create “idols” of SCP–2774–A, these included&nbsp;
amateur sculptures made of hoarded garbage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.440
images drawn of the sloth with any&nbsp;
materials they could get their hands on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:54.480
or even writing obsessively about the sloth.
Dr. Chung speculated that this behavior was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:59.680
perhaps an act of appeasement on the victims’&nbsp;
part, hoping to somehow sate the Slow Burn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:04.080
Sloth and lessen its effects on them through&nbsp;
worship. However, she would later find out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:09.840
the truth of the matter was far more disturbing.
Initially, due to their largely docile states,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:15.600
the subjects imprisoned in Site-116 were given&nbsp;
a relatively long leash. The subjects were even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.560
allocated two hours a day for social interaction&nbsp;
with fellow subjects at mealtimes and during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.280
a designated recreational period. During&nbsp;
these times, the subjects would often trade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:30.800
their Slow Burn Sloth effigies with one another.&nbsp;
However, Dr. Chung revoked the social interaction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:35.600
periods and began confining the subjects&nbsp;
to separate Euclid-class containment cells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:41.040
when violence began to break out between them.
It became clear that, during their 150-second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:46.720
periods of lucidity every 24-hours, the&nbsp;
subjects would become extremely distressed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:51.520
agitated, and even aggressive.
Dr. Chung also ordered any idols,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:56.560
from trash sculptures to doodles and notes on&nbsp;
fragmented scraps of paper, to be destroyed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:01.820
immediately. At its new increased power, the&nbsp;
Foundation became concerned that SCP–2774–A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:08.320
may develop the power to manifest through these&nbsp;
images. No meaningful headway was being made on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:13.680
a cure for the condition, so something needed&nbsp;
to be done before the situation got out of hand.&nbsp;

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:18.720
In hopes of gaining a better understanding of the&nbsp;
internal processes of Slow Burn Sloth victims,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:22.000
Dr. Chung decided to conduct a&nbsp;
series of interviews with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:29.920
subjects under her care. Two such subjects&nbsp;
- Subject-0866, aka David, and Subject-7444,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:36.800
aka Claire – were isolated for a 24-hour period,&nbsp;
in hopes of catching them during their daily 150&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:42.320
seconds of lucidity. Dr. Chung and the Foundation&nbsp;
found the results of these two interviews to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:48.000
as illuminating as they were utterly terrifying.
When David regained lucidity, he was in a state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:53.760
of extreme agitation and showed an unsettling&nbsp;
fixation on the clock in the Site-116 interview&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:58.960
room. Under direct questioning from Dr. Chung,&nbsp;
he revealed that Slow Burn Sloth victims are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:03.680
fully aware of what’s happening during their&nbsp;
zombified periods. He compared the sensation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:09.280
to being a passenger, trapped and bound in a&nbsp;
vehicle over which they have no control. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.720
in this state, victims are also unable to hold a&nbsp;
thought consistently for longer than five seconds.&nbsp;

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:20.640
This leaves them in an almost constant state&nbsp;
of disorientation. Worse still, David described&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.840
that victims are subjected to near-constant&nbsp;
hallucinations of the original sloth image,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:30.160
guiding and controlling their&nbsp;
movements. Almost like a puppeteer.&nbsp;

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:34.720
Thanks to the clock, David was aware of when&nbsp;
his 150 seconds of lucidity were about to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:40.320
come to an end. After apologizing for what he&nbsp;
was about to do, David lunged at Dr. Chung,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:45.520
causing a guard present in the interview room&nbsp;
to shoot him dead for Dr. Chung’s protection.&nbsp;

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:51.520
Dr. Chung’s interview with Claire echoed this same&nbsp;
sentiment. During her 150 seconds of lucidity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:57.120
Claire first begged to be killed, before divulging&nbsp;
further details about the zombification state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:02.400
She would describe hallucinations of the Slow Burn&nbsp;
Sloth stalking her constantly, and controlling her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:07.440
movements. In some cases, the Sloth would&nbsp;
force her to open her eyes all night, while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:13.840
it stands next to her bed and screams at her.
As Claire’s 150 seconds of lucidity ended and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:19.120
she became non-responsive, Dr. Chung put&nbsp;
in a request for Claire’s termination – a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:25.360
request that was fulfilled three days later.
The third interview with Subject-9225, also known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:32.320
as Jason, showed that SCP–2774–A appeared to be&nbsp;
manually starting the fights between the subjects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:38.240
– perhaps even for its own sadistic amusement. He&nbsp;
also stated, before the interview’s conclusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:43.680
that the image of the sloth in his hallucinations&nbsp;
was becoming darker and more tangible. Almost like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:49.360
it was becoming a real, physical being,&nbsp;
which was an unprecedented phenomenon.&nbsp;

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:53.840
Dr. Chung was, for the first&nbsp;
time in a while, truly afraid.&nbsp;

00:11:53.840 --> 00:12:00.480
It seemed, by all accounts, that SCP–2774–A’s&nbsp;
power was growing considerably as a result&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:05.600
of its huge number of active victims. Its&nbsp;
infection rate had likely risen well above 40%,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:11.600
and its ability to manifest would likely be on&nbsp;
the rise, too. If the Slow Burn Sloth was able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:18.880
manifest on a national broadcast, millions would&nbsp;
be infected, to truly apocalyptic results. Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:25.120
Chung only saw one solution that might curtail the&nbsp;
entity’s growing power, but it wouldn’t be pretty.&nbsp;

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:31.920
She devised a program known as Procedure-XXJ9.
As part of the procedure, additional staff were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:36.960
brought into Site-116 immediately. The real&nbsp;
purpose of the plan was revealed shortly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:42.720
afterward: To reduce the number of active&nbsp;
subjects on-site from 6,400 to a mere 200&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:48.000
in hopes of reducing risk. Over the next&nbsp;
several days, staff at Site-116 engaged in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:54.240
the gruesome task of executing around 6,200&nbsp;
infected subjects via lethal injection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.240 --> 00:13:00.720
This was an atrocity so horrific, even by SCP&nbsp;
Foundation standards, that Dr. Chung allowed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:05.440
parties involved to use Class-A Amnestics&nbsp;
to erase their memories of being involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:11.200
in the mass murder of Site-116’s subjects.
In the aftermath of the cull, the Foundation did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:18.960
report a decrease in SCP–2774–A’s manifestations&nbsp;
– so Dr. Chung’s procedure did indeed work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:23.840
just at a heavy human toll.
The tragic incident of the 2010 Harper Ridge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:30.640
SCP–2774 Containment Breach is a grim reminder&nbsp;
of just how far the SCP Foundation is willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:36.880
to go to do their job. And a reminder to be&nbsp;
careful where you look, because some images&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:43.280
have a much more lasting impact than others…
Now go check out “SCP-5049 - The Skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:47.680
Salesman - Demon Dan's Discount Homunculus&nbsp;
Depot” and “The Secret at the Bottom of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:53.600
SCP-087 - EXPLAINED” for more frightening&nbsp;
anomalous horrors from the SCP Foundation!

